3. Big.LITTLE Cluster Topology & Thread AffinityThe ChallengeHeterogeneous mobile System-on-Chips (SoCs) utilize power-saving cores alongside performance cores. The Android Linux kernel scheduler often shifts heavy computational threads onto low-power efficiency cores to prioritize thermals, causing inconsistent inference times (varying from 200ms to 1800ms).The OptimizationCTranslate2 execution threads are explicitly bound to high-performance cores using POSIX CPU affinity masks (sched_setaffinity).C++#include <sched.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <unistd.h>

void bind_thread_to_performance_cluster() {
    cpu_set_t cpuset;
    CPU_ZERO(&cpuset);

    // Standard 8-core SoC topology (Cores 0-3: Efficiency, Cores 4-7: Performance)
    int num_cores = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_CONF);
    if (num_cores >= 8) {
        CPU_SET(4, &cpuset);
        CPU_SET(5, &cpuset);
        CPU_SET(6, &cpuset);
        CPU_SET(7, &cpuset);
    } else {
        for (int i = num_cores / 2; i < num_cores; ++i) {
            CPU_SET(i, &cpuset);
        }
    }

    pthread_t current_thread = pthread_self();
    pthread_setaffinity_np(current_thread, sizeof(cpu_set_t), &cpuset);
}
